# Local working rules, loaded by any Claude Code session here and never published.
CLAUDE.local.md

# Agent governance store: role memory, sweep logs, warm-resume journals. Internal working
# material for whoever maintains this repo with an AI agent — never part of the published
# standard, never meant for a reader of the doc. Untracked-but-not-ignored here would let a
# routine `git add -A` publish it to this repo's public GitHub remote.
.claude/
.agents/

# Scratch/working files from agent sessions (drafts, throwaway probes). Same reasoning as
# .claude/ above: internal, never published, and this repo has a real remote to leak onto.
scratchpad/

# CoalBoard's own staging and reports (.coalboard/proposed/, .coalboard/reports/): a board's
# output lands inside the scanned repo by rule and is read there, never shipped.
.coalboard/

# The maintainer's publishing runbook (how this repository is published to its reading site: accounts, spaces,
# sync settings). It is working material for whoever maintains the repository, never part of the published standard.
# An untracked file that is not ignored is one `git add -A` from this repository's public remote, and an exclude that
# lives only in one clone is lost with the clone, so the line is here.
PUBLISHING.md
